Make GPUI's touch pan follow the scroll containers under a touch, as Flutter's scrollables each add their drag
recognizer, and keep taps and long presses to Flutter's touch slop.

What (needs 0044): a div that scrolls reports its axes while the touch's `Started` is dispatched
(`Window::scroll_container_under_touch`, next to `hold_scroll`), the touch route joins them (`PanAxes`: no container,
one axis, both), and the recognizer's pending touch accepts its pan by them. Only containers on one axis: the travel
along that axis past the hit slop, monodrag.dart's `VerticalDragGestureRecognizer` /
`HorizontalDragGestureRecognizer._hasSufficientGlobalDistanceToAccept`, and the pan locks to that axis. No container,
a two-axis one or both kinds: the pan rule as before (any direction past the touch slop, locked to the dominant axis).
`list()` reports its one axis, y, the same way (it scrolls only vertically). Since a pending touch no longer means
"within the slop", it keeps Flutter's tap and long-press slop apart from the pan's acceptance (`PressSlop`:
`PrimaryPointerGestureRecognizer`'s `preAcceptSlopTolerance`, `kTouchSlop`): once it strays past the touch slop from
where it went down it can no longer tap or long-press (and a double tap's first tap is dropped), while the on-axis pan
or a competing drag can still win it.

Why: without the containers' axes the pan took every move past 18 px in any direction, so a field's competing drag
(0044) lost sideways moves to the list it sits in: on desktop rows a `TouchDragKind::Pan` drag (36 px pan slop)
never won inside a vertical list. With them a pending touch no longer means "within the slop", so without
`PressSlop` a sideways swipe in a vertical list ended as a tap on its row.

Test: `gestures::recognizer_tests::flutter_recognizer_tests_pass`: rows gain a `container` (a canvas that reports a
scroll axis, as a scrolling div does): the tap_and_drag_test.dart rows run in a vertical container (their
`VerticalDragGestureRecognizer`), with "TapAndPanGestureRecognizer beats VerticalDragGestureRecognizer on a
horizontal pan", which needs it; drag_test.dart's horizontal-drag-with-competitor rows in a horizontal one; 2
monodrag rows (a one-axis container's pan accepts only on its axis), a GPUI row (a Pan-kind field drag in a vertical
list wins a horizontal drag) and 3 press-slop rows (in a vertical container 40 px sideways then release is no tap,
held past the deadline is no long press; a stray within the slop still taps). `gestures::tests::pan_axes_join_…`
tables how containers combine; `elements::list::test::test_list_scrolls_on_y_so_a_row_wins_a_sideways_drag`. Run:
`scripts/patch-test.sh recognizer`.

Upstream: not filed (patch rule 14).

